  "implementation": [
    "Unparsed letter-spacing and word-spacing values reuse native LengthPercentage::parse_string, with full-input consumption supplied by the native Parse trait.",
    "Standalone percentages use the native percentage token directly, avoiding serialization and reparsing. Mixed expressions use the shared native length-percentage parser.",
    "The existing native math-type guard rejects number-valued calculations where a length/percentage is required. Negative spacing remains valid.",
    "The text property handler uses existing length_percentage_to_text_spacing conversion and the existing TextSpacing model. Absolute lengths and percentage coefficients remain separate, so inherited percentages use the recipient used font size.",
    "Existing typed normal/length handling stays in its original path. Eligibility checks for the new native fallback are cached during stylesheet preparation.",
    "No Lightning CSS changes, parallel CSS grammar or renderer/GPUI changes were introduced."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Mixed non-linear math that cannot be represented by the existing two-component TextSpacing converter is still rejected by that converter. This does not implement every CSS Text math expression.",
    "Font-metric-dependent lengths keep existing resolution requirements.",
    "The 16 computed/valid helper outcomes establish syntax acceptance, not computed-value equality or pixel-level WPT passes."
  ],
